---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const scripts = `{
  "scripts": {
    "test": "vitest run",
    "test:generate": "GENERATOR_TEST=generate vitest run"
  }
}`;

const suite = `import { langiumGeneratorSuite } from 'langium-tools/testing';
import { createMyDslServices } from '../src/language/my-dsl-module';

langiumGeneratorSuite('./test-workspaces', {
  createServices: (context) => createMyDslServices(context),
  generateForModel: async (_services, model, gen) => {
    gen.createFile('out/' + model.name + '.ts', render(model));
  },
});`;

const tree = `test-workspaces/
  lights/
    dsls/
      room.mydsl
    generated/
      out/Room.ts
    generated-metadata.json
  doors/
    dsls/
      door.mydsl
    generated/
      out/Door.ts
    generated-metadata.json`;

const one = `import { GeneratorMode, langiumGeneratorTest } from 'langium-tools/testing';

await langiumGeneratorTest('./test-workspaces/lights', {
  createServices: (context) => createMyDslServices(context),
  generateForModel: async (_services, model, gen) => {
    gen.createFile('out/' + model.name + '.ts', render(model));
  },
  generateMode: GeneratorMode.Verify,
});`;

const custom = `import { getDocumentIssueSummary } from 'langium-tools/base';

function validateDocuments(services, documents) {
  for (const doc of documents) {
    const summary = getDocumentIssueSummary(doc);
    expect(summary.countErrors, summary.message).toBe(0);
  }
}

langiumGeneratorSuite('./test-workspaces', {
  createServices: (context) => createMyDslServices(context),
  validateDocuments,
  generateForModel: async (_services, model, gen) => {
    gen.createFile('out/' + model.name + '.java', renderJava(model), { target: 'java' });
    gen.createFile('src/' + model.name + '.java', stub(model), { target: 'java', overwrite: false });
  },
}, [
  { name: 'java', overwrite: true },
]);`;

const meta = `{
  "generatedFiles": [
    { "filename": "out/Room.ts", "overwrite": true },
    { "filename": "src/Room.ts", "overwrite": false }
  ]
}`;
---
<Base
  title="Generator tests — langium-tools"
  description="Snapshot-test Langium generators by committing the generated tree and comparing it in CI. Regenerate when the change is intentional."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <header class="doc-hero container">
      <div class="kicker">langium-tools/testing</div>
      <h1>Generator tests</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Generated code is part of the contract. Commit it. The test builds a real
        Langium workspace, runs your generator in memory, and checks every file.
        When you mean to change the output, regenerate and review the diff.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
      <h2>Two modes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Verify</b> — the default. In-memory output must match the committed files, byte for byte, and the overwrite flags must match the metadata.</li>
        <li><b>Generate</b> — <span class="inline-code">GENERATOR_TEST=generate</span>. The <span class="inline-code">generated/</span> directory is replaced and the metadata file is rewritten.</li>
      </ul>
      <CodeBlock code={scripts} lang="json" filename="package.json" />
      <p>
        <span class="inline-code">npm test</span> is what CI runs.
        <span class="inline-code">npm run test:generate</span> is what you run locally
        after an intentional generator change. Then <span class="inline-code">git diff</span>
        and commit.
      </p>

      <h2>One test per workspace</h2>
      <p>
        <span class="inline-code">langiumGeneratorSuite</span> adds a Vitest test for each
        immediate subdirectory. <span class="inline-code">createServices</span> receives
        <span class="inline-code">NodeFileSystem</span> from <span class="inline-code">langium/node</span>.
        When you use <span class="inline-code">generateForModel</span>, the service object
        must have exactly one entry besides <span class="inline-code">shared</span>.
        That is the usual Langium shape: <span class="inline-code">{`{ MyDsl, shared }`}</span>.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock code={suite} filename="generator.test.ts" />

      <h3>Directory layout</h3>
      <p>
        Put DSL files in <span class="inline-code">dsls/</span>. The runner looks for that
        name before it deletes anything, so a wrong path cannot wipe an unrelated folder.
        Generated files land in <span class="inline-code">generated/</span>. With the default
        target, metadata is <span class="inline-code">generated-metadata.json</span> next to
        <span class="inline-code">dsls/</span>.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock code={tree} lang="text" filename="test-workspaces" />

      <h2>What the default pipeline does</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><b>initWorkspace</b> — <span class="inline-code">WorkspaceManager.initializeWorkspace</span> on the test directory.</li>
        <li><b>buildDocuments</b> — every document Langium loaded, built with validation on.</li>
        <li><b>validateDocuments</b> — fails the test if the DSL has lexer or parser errors. Validation diagnostics are not treated as failures here, so a workspace can legally contain warnings.</li>
        <li><b>generate</b> — <span class="inline-code">generateForModel</span> for each document, or your own <span class="inline-code">generateForWorkspace</span> if generation is not one-file-at-a-time.</li>
        <li><b>compare or write</b> — verify mode reads the tree. Generate mode replaces it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Any of those steps can be replaced on the options object.</p>

      <h2>A single workspace, from any test runner</h2>
      <p>
        <span class="inline-code">langiumGeneratorTest</span> does not call Vitest's
        <span class="inline-code">test()</span>. Use it when you want one workspace inside
        a test you wrote yourself. The assertions still use Vitest's <span class="inline-code">expect</span>.
        <span class="inline-code">using</span>, from the same entry, runs a function with a
        value and returns that value.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock code={one} filename="one-workspace.test.ts" />

      <h2>Custom targets and stricter validation</h2>
      <p>
        Pass targets as the third argument. Once any target is passed, every target
        is written that way, including the default one:
        <span class="inline-code">generated/DEFAULT/</span> with
        <span class="inline-code">DEFAULT-metadata.json</span>, and
        <span class="inline-code">generated/&lt;name&gt;/</span> with
        <span class="inline-code">&lt;name&gt;-metadata.json</span>.
        With no extra targets, files stay in <span class="inline-code">generated/</span>
        and the metadata file is <span class="inline-code">generated-metadata.json</span>.
        The check fails when a file is missing, unexpected, different, or when its
        overwrite flag changed.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock code={custom} filename="java-target.test.ts" />

      <h3>Metadata</h3>
      <p>
        The JSON is how a change from "generate once" to "always overwrite" shows up in
        review even when the file bytes stayed the same.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock code={meta} lang="json" filename="generated-metadata.json" />

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          Verify mode never writes. A failing test leaves the committed tree as it was,
          and the message names the file, the target, and whether the mismatch is content,
          a missing file, an extra file, or the overwrite flag.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        API: <a href={`${SITE.typedoc}/functions/testing.langiumGeneratorSuite.html`}>langiumGeneratorSuite</a>,
        <a href={`${SITE.typedoc}/functions/testing.langiumGeneratorTest.html`}>langiumGeneratorTest</a>,
        <a href={`${SITE.typedoc}/interfaces/testing.GeneratorTestOptions.html`}>GeneratorTestOptions</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="next-guides">
        <a href="/generator/">← Code generation</a>
        <a href="/matchers/">Vitest matchers →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
